Verification
DB ensure: boot course-service; confirm log course_certificates table ensured and the table exists (SHOW TABLES LIKE 'course_certificates').
First download assigns 0001: as a user who has completed a certificate-enabled course and has no row yet, call GET /api/certificates/course/:courseId → response includes certificateNumber: "0001"; a row appears in course_certificates with cert_seq=1.
Stable on re-download: call the same endpoint again → still 0001, no new row, counter not advanced.
Second learner gets 0002: a different completed user on the same course → 0002.
Per-course independence: a completed user on a different course → that course's own 0001.
progress/course echoes it: GET /api/progress/course/:courseId for a user who already has a number returns the same certificateNumber; for a completed user who has not opened the certificate yet it returns null (and no row is created by the progress call — verify the row count is unchanged after hitting progress).
Concurrency: fire two simultaneous first-time certificate fetches for the same new user+course (or two different new users on the same course); confirm no duplicate cert_seq and exactly one row per user (unique keys hold; bounded retry resolves the race).
Frontend: open the certificate modal on a completed course → the layout shows the real serial (e.g. 0001) instead of 4987; the printed/PNG certificate carries it.